" Oooooh wow. She's the killer? Didn't see that that one coming did we Steve?" Jeremy shouted.
& nbsp;
" Noooo. What a twist. Just like the gun she was holding. Of course, **one** of us would get shot, and I'm not the main character, so go figure." Steve replied, clutching the gunshot wound in his stomach. The two of them had stumbled right into the delicately laid, unforeseeable trap, laid for them by Jeremy's own, sweet, seemingly non-psychotic wife.
& nbsp;
" I mean. It's not like we set up the meeting down the road from the emergency room, is it Jez?" exclaimed Steve, still clutching the unforeseeable gunshot wound in his chest, " So it's in my chest now! La-di-da, look at me with my moving gunshot wound, am I right Jez?"
& nbsp;
" Damn straight Steve." Jeremy confirmed. Seeing that he was perfectly single again, Jeremy quipped, " Looks like we're going on the town tonight? Except we're not though, are we. He's got a gunshot wound that can't make up it's mind on where it is, and I've just had to shoot my insane wife of 15 years through the skull, most likely emotionally scarring me for life, after she tried to kill me, so I wouldn't'find the hidden treasure'." Jeremy had *somehow* managed to find out about the treasure, that would be the cliffhanger for the next book.
& nbsp;
" Nice one Jez!" reassured Steve, from across the road, still clutching the emotional kick in the knackers that was his gunshot wound, " I mean, I haven't even been described as bleeding out in any way, yet, so I've got all the time in the world!" The duo reflected on the last two weeks. They'd definitely be getting promotions.
& nbsp;
" 13 people are dead!" shouted Jeremy, " Who in God's name would promote *us*?!" The two, were, clearly upset, about the turn of events? And they would. Be. Going their separate ways. Soon, I think.
& nbsp;
" Yeah sure. After all that we'll go our separate ways. For no particular reason. You know what Steve, I don't doubt we'll be reunited under some hilarious circumstances for the next book, when we search for this treasure!" cried Jeremy.
& nbsp;
